# Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2016) — the two capacitive keys under the glass
#
# They are not keys of their own: the ST FTS touchscreen controller reports
# them as a two-bit bitmap inside its own event stream, and the mainline
# driver (drivers/input/touchscreen/stmfts.c, stmfts_report_key_event)
# names those bits after the ST reference design, not after Samsung's
# printed legends:
#
#     bit 0x01 -> KEY_MENU  (139)
#     bit 0x02 -> KEY_BACK  (158)
#
# On THIS panel the physical mapping was measured with getevent -lt,
# pressing the keys one at a time (21/09):
#
#     LEFT key   -> KEY_BACK 158   legend: recents (⧉)
#     RIGHT key  -> KEY_MENU 139   legend: back    (◁)
#
# That is, the driver names are swapped with respect to the glass, and on
# top of that the left key is not a "menu": it is the recent-apps key.
# Without this file Android reads Generic.kl and gets left=BACK,
# right=MENU — which in Launcher3 opens the wallpaper/widget panel, the
# symptom this started from.
#
# The file is chosen by the input device's NAME: EventHub looks for
# <canonical name>.kl (InputDeviceIdentifier::getCanonicalName in
# frameworks/native/libs/input/InputDevice.cpp) under /product, /system_ext,
# /odm, /vendor. The device is called "stmfts", hence stmfts.kl.
#
# The fix is made HERE and not in the kernel on purpose: the stmfts driver
# is generic and mainline, the legends belong to this tablet.

key 158   APP_SWITCH
key 139   BACK
